      ":question/problem": "Differentiate $2 x^{2}cos⁡(x).$\n\n$(2 x^{2}cos⁡(x))^{′}=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,2 x^{2}sin⁡(x)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=2 x^{2}$ and $v(x)=cos⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2 x^{2}cos⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2 x^{2})^{′}\\cdot cos⁡(x)+2 x^{2}\\cdot (cos⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =(4 x)(cos⁡(x))+(2 x^{2})(-sin⁡(x)) \\\\  & =4 xcos⁡(x)-2 x^{2}sin⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
